[Service](/lore/services-capture-dependencies) monitoring needs all four golden signals. Separate symptom detection from internal diagnosis, and distinguish failed-request latency from successful latency.

> The four golden signals of monitoring are latency, traffic, errors, and saturation.

Source: [Q18](/lore/durability-bibliography#q18); [B8](/lore/durability-bibliography#b8-monitoring-distributed-systems).

## Failure it prevents

A service reports fast responses while errors rise or scarce capacity is exhausted.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Metric.counter`, gauge, and histogram supply instruments. Connect backlog and parked-work observations through the actual adapters. Define alerts and response outside these constructors.

Source: `packages/effect/src/Metric.ts`.

## How to check

Create a slow dependency and a parked item. Verify that user-visible failure and resource saturation are observable. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Dead letters need a return path](/lore/dead-letters-need-a-return-path), [Admission control protects recovery](/lore/admission-controls-new-work).

